      "receiptSource": "Original Receipt in \u0027\u003Ci\u003EThe Forme of Cury\u003C/i\u003E\u0027 by the Chief Master-Cook of King Richard II, c1390 (\u003Ca href=\u0022references.html#cury-1390\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003ECury 1390\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E)",
      "receiptText": "\u003Cb\u003EFLAUMPENS\u003C/b\u003E\u003Cbr\u003E\nTake fat Pork salted, scrape it clean, grynde it small. Grynde cheese \u0026 do thereto with sugur and good \u003Ca href=\u0022spice-powders.html\u0022\u003E\u003Cb\u003Epowders\u003C/b\u003E\u003C/a\u003E. Make a coffyn [casing] of an inch deep and do this forcemeat therin, make a thin foile of good paste \u0026 carve out theroff small poyntes, fry them in forcemeat. \u0026 bake it up \u0026amp;c\u003Cbr\u003E"
    }
